course: dictionary
lesson: 13711
title: Words about time
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how fast something happens. Instantaneous means happening straight away, with no delay at all. «The alarm gave an instantaneous beep the moment the door opened.» The beep came at once, so instantaneous must mean with no waiting.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Phrases like «the moment» or «straight away» show that something is instant. Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word such as instant or immediate. If it still makes sense, you have the right idea. «The reply was almost instantaneous» means very quick, but not quite the same second.
explain: Maths and science use instantaneous in a special way. Instantaneous speed is the speed at one exact moment, like the number on a speedometer. Average speed is the speed for a whole journey, and the two can be very different.
fact: Instantaneous is an adjective. Its adverb is instantaneously: «The screen changed instantaneously.»
fact: Instantaneous means happening immediately, with no delay at all.
fact: In science, instantaneous means at one exact instant of time, as in «instantaneous speed».
fact: Light from a nearby lamp seems to arrive instantaneously, though it actually takes a tiny amount of time.
fact: Average speed is for a whole journey; instantaneous speed is for one single moment.
exercise: «The doorbell gave an instantaneous ring as soon as I pressed it.» What does instantaneous mean? | Very loud and long | Happening slowly over many hours | *Happening at once, with no delay | Broken and silent
exercise: «The speedometer showed the car's instantaneous speed at that moment.» What does instantaneous speed mean? | The speed that is always the same | *The speed at one exact moment | The average speed for the whole trip | The speed of a snail
exercise: Find the word in «The screen changed instantaneously» that tells you how it changed. | changed | the | *instantaneously | screen
test: Mia says her reply to the message was instantaneous, but she took five minutes to type it. What is wrong? | Five minutes is instantaneous because it is quick | Instantaneous means slow | *Five minutes is a delay, so the reply was not instantaneous | Nothing is wrong with her reply
test: Which sentence describes an instantaneous reaction? | *Her hand pulled back from the hot pan at once, before she even thought about it | She waited until the next day to say ouch | The pan was cold, so she never touched it | She thought about it for an hour, then moved her hand
exam: What does instantaneous mean in «The reply was instantaneous»? | *Happening at once, with no delay | Covered in dust | Long and boring | Hard to understand
